# Review — Side A (interim_v1, production default) — Tech House Heldout

## TL;DR
- **Tracks:** 9 (Arielle Free, Idris Elba - Cause I Can excluded: 16ms off its own kicks on the beatgrid gate, likely Afro/Latin-influenced rhythm outside the detector's straight 4-to-floor range).
- **Transitions:** 8. **Loops:** 5, all quality 0.58-0.65 (clean, well clear of the 0.20 gate and the 0.20-0.30 borderline-for-ears band).
- **Chop corrections applied this run:** none needed — every track's stem detection matched its stem panels on first pass.
- **Structural finding, not a defect:** Enzo Is Burning - All The Ladies has no outro at all (drums/bass/vocals/other are all still at full energy on the very last bar of the file — a genuine cold ending, confirmed visually, not a detection miss). The pipeline handled it correctly: T8 uses a full 24-bar STANDARD crossfade with proper volume automation, so Enzo fades out in the mix even though the source audio itself never fades.
- **Style spread:** 1 quick_swap (17 bars, T2), 3 standard (24-33 bars, T3/T5/T8), 4 long_blend (40-56 bars, T1/T4/T6/T7).
- **BPM:** all 9 tracks sit within 128.03-131.02 BPM (tight pool); no tempo arc used for this experimental build (per Phase 3.5's own design — MixPlan/TempoContract only applies to production builds with `--tempo-arc`).
- **Listen for:** T8 (Enzo -> Jewel Kid) is the one genuinely unusual transition in this set — Enzo has no natural handoff point, so the mix swaps mid-drop. This is the transition most worth your ear.
- **Pipeline confidence:** high. All chops verified visually against stem panels, all hints agreed with sections (34/34 checks, 0 errors/warnings), all 8 transitions read clean, all 5 loops clean.
- **Output:** `Output/AB/A/Mix A.als` (interim_v1 policy — the same rulebook every production mix uses today).

## Per-track section sanity (Phase 1d)

All 9 DETECT pictures reviewed against their 4-stem panels (drums/bass/vocals/other). Zero corrections needed.

| Track | Verdict | Note |
|---|---|---|
| Yellody feat Lovelee - No Time To Stop | ✓ chops clean | Sustained bass-only DJ outro (drums+bass run, vocals/other tail off) |
| Freejak - Know You Better | ✓ chops clean | Sustained bass-only outro |
| HARTY - There's A Party Going On | ✓ chops clean | Two short mid-track fills, both correctly labelled |
| Jay de Lys - Loaded Clipz | ✓ chops clean | 8-bar cameo drop_1 into a 16-bar build before the full drop_2; most complex structure in the set (12 raw sections) |
| Sam Leagas - Bad Behaviours | ✓ chops clean | Sustained bass-only outro |
| Sapian, Aviv Sab - Deep House Pumpin' | ✓ chops clean | Sustained bass-only outro |
| Marco Lys, Michael Ekow - Super Hot | ✓ chops clean | Short (9-bar) but genuine tail-off outro |
| Enzo Is Burning - All The Ladies | ✓ chops clean | **No outro section exists** — confirmed cold ending, not a miss |
| Jewel Kid - Talking to You | ✓ chops clean | Genuine fade-out outro (drums+bass both decline), unlike the sustained ones elsewhere |

## Per-transition table (Phase 4a, FULL view)

| # | Transition | Overlap | Style | Loop | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| T1 | Yellody -> Freejak | 40 bars | long_blend | out tail 116-124 x4 | ✓ aligned |
| T2 | Freejak -> HARTY | 17 bars | quick_swap | none | ✓ aligned |
| T3 | HARTY -> Jay de Lys | 32 bars | standard | out tail 0-8 x3 | ✓ aligned |
| T4 | Jay de Lys -> Sam Leagas | 48 bars | long_blend | out tail 800-832 x2 | ✓ aligned |
| T5 | Sam Leagas -> Sapian | 33 bars | standard | none | ✓ aligned |
| T6 | Sapian -> Marco Lys | 56 bars | long_blend | out tail 640-672 x1 | ✓ aligned |
| T7 | Marco Lys -> Enzo | 56 bars | long_blend | out tail 608-640 x1 | ✓ aligned |
| T8 | Enzo -> Jewel Kid | 24 bars | standard | none | ✓ aligned — see note above |

8/8 transitions pass. 9/9 track chops pass.

## Loop quality (Phase 4b)

| # | Track | Region | Quality | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| L01 | Yellody | 2 bars x4 | 0.65 | ✓ clean |
| L02 | HARTY | 2 bars x3 | 0.62 | ✓ clean |
| L03 | Jay de Lys | 8 bars x2 | 0.62 | ✓ clean |
| L04 | Sapian | 8 bars x1 | 0.64 | ✓ clean |
| L05 | Marco Lys | 8 bars x1 | 0.58 | ✓ clean |

5/5 loops clean. None in the 0.20-0.30 borderline band; none flagged for special ear attention beyond the general listen.

## Gates run

- `validate_hints_vs_sections.py`: **PASS**, 34/34 checks, 0 errors, 0 warnings.
- `validate_als.py` (post-automation, `--require-devices --expected-tracks 9`): **PASS**, structurally valid, Ableton can load it.
- No render exists yet, so `render_check.py` has not run — do that once Sam bounces `Mix A.als` in Ableton.

## Known limitations of this run

- No Mixed In Key metadata (MIK's UI automation failed on this machine — a known-machine issue, not a pipeline defect). Sequencing fell back to BPM-only ordering; no Camelot harmonic scoring is available for this set. Does not affect BPM/grid accuracy, which comes from the owned stem-grid detector regardless of MIK.
- This is the Phase 3.5 experimental comparison build (Side A of a 3-way policy test), not a MixPlan/tempo-arc production build — no `TempoContract`, no Phase 3b reconciliation gate. That's by design for this phase.
- Two real, narrowly-scoped bugs were found and fixed in the pipeline while building this (both regression-tested): a cross-project stem-cache lookup that failed closed instead of resolving correctly (`apply_loops.py`), and a librosa API version mismatch plus a missing BPM fallback in the loop-review picture generator (`loop_review_viz.py`). Neither affected Side A's actual arrangement or automation — both were review/tooling gaps.
