**Learning loop actually fed, for the first time:** re-ran the now-fixed `learn_from_correction.py` against Sam's real House 10 correction pair - previously vacuous (the exact bug the burn item existed to fix). 9 real transitions now in `Documentation/Mix Patterns Library/pair_history.jsonl` (5 individually ground-truth-verified this session).

**SAM_V2 candidate designed, reviewed, built, reviewed again, merged:** the swap-at-drop-end pattern maps onto an ALREADY-BUILT but never-enabled mechanism (`CUE_CONFIG.incoming_intro_loop`, built 2026-08-17 from a different correction pair, Fresh Mix V2, matching 5/6 transitions there too - independent corroboration, not a new hypothesis). Plan reviewed by Codex + MiniMax BEFORE any code (PROCEED-WITH-CHANGES: caught that this mechanism and the existing `extend_incoming_entry` could silently corrupt each other, and that a naive density gate would be a no-op dressed as a fix). Implemented on `feat/sam-v2-candidate`: mutual exclusion between the two incoming-intro mechanisms (a REAL bug, not just a gap - both produced the same spec kind and the second silently overwrote the first while both physically prepended clips), shadow-only density instrumentation (measures, does not gate this round - deliberately), wired `build_ab_comparison.py` to actually enable the flag for the first time, fixed a real separate bug in `seal_listening_test.py` (claimed metadata stripping, actually used `shutil.copyfile`). Round-2 code review (Codex + an independent Claude subagent, both executing against the live worktree) found ANOTHER real bug via independently-constructed counterexamples: a density baseline documented as "median" that actually computed whole-track RMS (outlier-sensitive) - fixed, verified against both reviewers' reproduced counterexamples. The subagent went further unprompted: found real gitignored Fresh Mix V2 fixtures still on disk, re-ran the fix against real production data, confirmed it holds there too. Merged to `main`; the merge itself exposed a benign frozen-baseline schema mismatch (`test_alignment_baseline.py` predated two new dataclass fields) - verified purely additive (292 insertions, 0 deletions, zero decision drift) before refreshing.

**Held-out material:** the two plan reviews disagreed on reusing the existing Stephanes Playlist replay set vs curating fresh material - surfaced to Sam rather than picked unilaterally. Sam chose fresh. Curated 10 Tech House tracks via the REAL samwillsmixing database (Neon Postgres, connection in `Sam-Wills-Mixing-Web-Site/v2/.env.local` - the Supabase MCP tried first was the wrong database entirely and timed out repeatedly), token-overlap-matched against local masters, created `Test Project/10.09.26 Tech House Heldout/Audio/` with the 10 copied in. Per Sam's explicit instruction, STOPPED before running any pipeline step (no MIK, no stem grids/Demucs, no section detection) - resumes next session.

**Key learnings:** (1) a reviewer's "SHIP-WITH-FIXES" is only as strong as its verification method - a review that couldn't execute (no shell/exec tool, or a sandboxed environment with no writable temp dir) produced weaker findings than one that could, twice this session, on both burn-round and SAM_V2 rounds; (2) when two independent reviewers construct their OWN counterexample and land on the identical bug, that's strong signal to fix immediately rather than debate; (3) before migrating a working mechanism's config into a "more consistent" architecture, check whether the existing pattern already solves the problem the migration is for - `CueConfig`'s `_apply_cue_signals` already had proper per-invocation isolation, so `incoming_intro_loop` stayed there rather than moving into `TransitionPolicy` as an earlier plan draft proposed.

