G:\Wired Masters Dropbox\Sam Wills\0.1---GIT HUB---\Obsidian Brain\Ecosystem\Reusable Assets.md:134:| Feed-forward mix prediction (bounce without bouncing) | Predicts a rendered mix's per-band level from SOURCE audio + the Ableton set alone, no export: per-band power = sum over tracks of (master*trim)^2 * gain(t)^2 * band_power(source with the low shelf APPLIED AS A FILTER), source instant via the clip's own warp markers. Every band under 0.5 dB mean error against a real 84-minute bounce. THREE TRANSFERABLE LESSONS BAKED IN: (1) the shelf must be a filter, not a per-band scalar, or it moves the top of the spectrum as much as the bottom; (2) score accuracy ONLY where a band is actually present - including silence inflated the apparent error nearly fourfold and hid the fact that the residual was a constant offset; (3) the model REFUSES (non-empty master chain, automated filter, filter resonance) rather than returning a plausible number for a path it cannot represent. Sizing asks whether the MOVE beats the ERROR BAR (>= 2x the band's p95), not whether a band is accurate in the abstract. | `Sam Wills/0.1---GIT HUB---/Automated DJ Mixes/Source/mix_predict.py` | Automated DJ Mixes | audio, ableton, validation | Live; 11 tests, 9 mutants killed | 2026-08-28 |
