G:\Wired Masters Dropbox\Sam Wills\0.1---GIT HUB---\Obsidian Brain\Ecosystem\Reusable Assets.md:145:| Real per-track tempo from Ableton project files | `extractRealTempo(source_path)` reads the ACTUAL session tempo Sam set, straight off disk, instead of guessing from genre or running audio-based beat detection: `.als` is gzip-compressed XML with a `<Tempo><Manual Value="140" /></Tempo>` element; the function resolves `source_path` (already stored in any track database) against whichever machine is running via `findDropboxPath()` (handles Sam's 3 machines having different drive letters), picks the latest `.als` by his own versioning convention, and parses it. Proven against 4 real, unrelated projects (a mix and a mastering-only job both worked). Every failure mode (no source_path, wrong-machine path, no `.als`, corrupt read) returns null gracefully. Any project with access to Sam's mix/master catalogue and a genre-guessed or missing BPM value should use this before building a detector or trusting a guess - confirmed one whole night of production renders were ALL running at the wrong tempo before this existed. | `Sam Wills/0.1---GIT HUB---/Wrens-Content-Engine/src/shared/audio/als-tempo.ts` | Wrens-Content-Engine | audio, ableton, ai-infra | Live; proven against 4 real projects, deployed across a 13-track production batch | 2026-09-10 |
